00:48:40.130 --> 00:48:43.890
I don't know that you try to avoid when you go to the mailbox.

847
00:48:44.570 --> 00:48:50.750
Well, we had a fan question in this scene from Tennille, who wants to know, in this episode,

848
00:48:50.970 --> 00:48:54.990
there are a lot of talking heads with Michael facing the window where it's snowing.

849
00:48:55.190 --> 00:49:00.870
Were those talking heads shot in sequence so that they didn't have to keep turning the snow on and off?

850
00:49:00.870 --> 00:49:04.070
Well, yes, yes.

851
00:49:04.070 --> 00:49:07.530
I love this question, Angela, because we've never really talked about this.

852
00:49:07.670 --> 00:49:11.710
We always shot all of our talking heads in a row.

853
00:49:12.150 --> 00:49:17.930
So what they would do is they would set up the shot, let's say, in Michael's office for a talking head.

854
00:49:18.050 --> 00:49:24.070
And every talking head he had for that episode, they would spend hours doing all of them.

855
00:49:24.070 --> 00:49:25.990
And the same thing in the conference room.

856
00:49:26.170 --> 00:49:32.270
Remember, they'd set up the chair and we would all cycle in for hours and do our talking heads.

857
00:49:32.690 --> 00:49:35.610
Yes, it would literally be like talking head day on set.

858
00:49:36.190 --> 00:49:39.870
And I always really felt for Steve because he always had the moSt.

859
00:49:40.110 --> 00:49:46.710
And I would think like, oh, my God, I had to like learn one, you know, and maybe they would give me some alts on the day.

860
00:49:47.170 --> 00:49:51.090
But Steve had to learn so many and just sit there and do them and do them.

861
00:49:51.090 --> 00:49:57.770
And Veda would be there, our script supervisor, and sometimes she would remind you if you had more than one.

862
00:49:57.890 --> 00:50:03.890
Okay, now remember, this talking head is after Dwight left, so you're more sad than the one before, you know?

863
00:50:04.070 --> 00:50:07.610
So sometimes she was helping us kind of navigate the time sequence of it all.

864
00:50:08.410 --> 00:50:08.690
Yes.

865
00:50:09.090 --> 00:50:15.370
And we would usually do these either first thing in the morning or at the end of the day.

866
00:50:15.630 --> 00:50:17.390
Steve would always do his first thing in the morning.

867
00:50:17.390 --> 00:50:19.070
I think he liked to lead with them.

868
00:50:19.310 --> 00:50:25.790
He would oftentimes, I feel like on a Monday, it would be like Steve talking heads until almost lunch.

869
00:50:25.970 --> 00:50:26.330
Yeah.

870
00:50:26.470 --> 00:50:30.790
And then we would all come in and film like group scenes for the rest of the day.

871
00:50:31.050 --> 00:50:31.230
Yeah.

872
00:50:31.830 --> 00:50:38.570
But then on Fridays, we would spend Friday afternoons all the rest of the cast doing our talking heads.

873
00:50:38.770 --> 00:50:40.670
That was kind of how we framed our week.

874
00:50:40.950 --> 00:50:42.330
Yeah, that's how I remember it too.

875
00:50:42.330 --> 00:50:47.370
Well, Jenna, you know, Oscar's back now and he walks back over to accounting.

