And in this one, Michael's like, what's up?

940
00:54:25.010 --> 00:54:26.410
And Andy goes, nerfin.

941
00:54:28.090 --> 00:54:28.570
Nerfin.

942
00:54:29.010 --> 00:54:29.490
Nerfin.

943
00:54:29.810 --> 00:54:33.570
Me and my kids are saying nerfin.

944
00:54:33.850 --> 00:54:36.350
It just, it has stuck here at the house.

945
00:54:36.490 --> 00:54:37.650
I thought it was so funny.

946
00:54:37.650 --> 00:54:43.590
But yeah, Andy's driving Michael crazy and Michael has a whole talking head from behind

947
00:54:43.590 --> 00:54:44.170
his door.

948
00:54:44.370 --> 00:54:45.030
He's hiding.

949
00:54:45.870 --> 00:54:51.750
It was, it made me laugh out loud because I didn't know where he was during this because

950
00:54:51.750 --> 00:54:53.890
Andy's looking for him and he's just nowhere.

951
00:54:53.890 --> 00:54:54.810
He's nowhere.

952
00:54:55.270 --> 00:54:59.770
And then when he's revealed to be giving this whole talking head from behind his door,

953
00:54:59.990 --> 00:55:05.350
one of the things I loved about it most was that while hiding, he was still compelled

954
00:55:05.350 --> 00:55:07.410
to perform and speak to the camera.

955
00:55:08.210 --> 00:55:15.350
He was like, I'm hiding, but I'm not going to stop presenting myself to this camera crew.

956
00:55:15.770 --> 00:55:19.930
I wonder if he was like, I'm going to hide and you have to too, because if Andy sees you

957
00:55:19.930 --> 00:55:24.170
guys in here, so like, is there a room where the camera crew is like smushed up against

958
00:55:24.170 --> 00:55:25.850
the wall, also hiding?

959
00:55:26.750 --> 00:55:28.070
That's such a good point.

960
00:55:28.250 --> 00:55:31.530
Like all Andy has to look for is like, where's the camera pointed?

961
00:55:31.810 --> 00:55:32.010
Yeah.

962
00:55:32.630 --> 00:55:35.230
There's a crew constantly following Michael around.

963
00:55:35.230 --> 00:55:40.990
Well, we're coming up on a scene that completely destroyed John Krasinski in real life.

964
00:55:41.170 --> 00:55:45.290
I don't think he's ever laughed so hard ever, ever on the show.

965
00:55:45.510 --> 00:55:48.210
He has said it's the hardest he laughed the whole series.

966
00:55:48.530 --> 00:55:50.630
Like, and I texted Creed about it.

967
00:55:50.890 --> 00:55:51.170
Yeah.

968
00:55:51.350 --> 00:55:55.750
It's this scene in the kitchen where Oscar comes in and he's just kind of like, where's

969
00:55:55.750 --> 00:55:56.310
Dwight?

970
00:55:56.650 --> 00:56:05.750
And Creed says Dwight was decapitated and they had a funeral for a bird, which is not

971
00:56:05.750 --> 00:56:06.230
correct.

972
00:56:06.470 --> 00:56:07.830
But kind of correct.

973
00:56:08.110 --> 00:56:10.090
Just all mushed up together.

974
00:56:10.450 --> 00:56:10.990
Yeah.

975
00:56:11.190 --> 00:56:14.970
Ed Truck was decapitated and they did have a funeral for a bird.

976
00:56:15.110 --> 00:56:17.850
And remember, Jim wasn't around for any of this.

977
00:56:18.030 --> 00:56:21.530
So Jim isn't even able to like correct this.

978
00:56:21.530 --> 00:56:25.130
So he just says, I'm pretty sure that's not real.

979
00:56:25.490 --> 00:56:28.730
And then Creed says, you're not real, man.

980
00:56:29.890 --> 00:56:33.450
And that is the line that destroyed John Krasinski.

981
00:56:33.970 --> 00:56:34.130
Yeah.

982
00:56:34.630 --> 00:56:37.070
John could not keep it together.

983
00:56:37.370 --> 00:56:40.330
He crumbled like into just bits of laughter.

984
00:56:40.330 --> 00:56:42.010
And I texted Creed.

985
00:56:42.150 --> 00:56:44.990
I was like, Creed, oh, my gosh, we're breaking down the return.

986
00:56:44.990 --> 00:56:48.550
And you have that great line that you said to John.

987
00:56:48.550 --> 00:56:50.610
And he was like, I said, what was that like?

988
00:56:50.670 --> 00:56:55.650
He said, oh, Ange, it was so much fun to see John lose it like that.

989
00:56:55.770 --> 00:56:57.850
He said he lost it.

990
00:56:58.330 --> 00:57:04.750
There are a couple of times on the show where John has laughed so hard that like you can't,

991
00:57:04.750 --> 00:57:10.690
you just can't even film him because when he really loses it, he cannot be brought back.

992
00:57:10.850 --> 00:57:11.530
He can't.

993
00:57:11.810 --> 00:57:13.610
He's like he is what we said.

994
00:57:13.730 --> 00:57:14.310
He is destroyed.

995
00:57:14.510 --> 00:57:14.930
He's destroyed.

996
00:57:15.050 --> 00:57:15.810
He doubles over.

997
00:57:16.030 --> 00:57:16.990
He kind of tears up.

998
00:57:17.070 --> 00:57:18.070
He can't make noise.

999
00:57:18.530 --> 00:57:20.710
It was laughing like that.

1000
00:57:20.850 --> 00:57:24.490
And I said, Creed, I mean, how did you how many takes did you do?

1001
00:57:24.590 --> 00:57:27.130
And he said, I think we got one where he kept it together.

1002
00:57:27.330 --> 00:57:28.850
I think that's the one they used.

1003
00:57:30.750 --> 00:57:31.590
Yeah, exactly.

1004
00:57:32.250 --> 00:57:32.670
Exactly.

1005
00:57:33.250 --> 00:57:38.750
So now we have this little scene where Michael is noticing that like the plant in the office

1006
00:57:38.750 --> 00:57:39.490
is dying.

1007
00:57:39.830 --> 00:57:43.690
He says, you need to talk to the cleaning crew about this.

1008
00:57:43.790 --> 00:57:48.230
And also, while you're at it, they used to arrange the toys on my desk in this really

1009
00:57:48.230 --> 00:57:49.110
pleasing way.

1010
00:57:49.330 --> 00:57:51.270
And I need to know why they've stopped.

1011
00:57:51.650 --> 00:57:54.410
And Pam is like, well, no, that was Dwight.

1012
00:57:55.210 --> 00:57:56.730
Dwight used to do that.

1013
00:57:57.170 --> 00:58:01.190
And then, of course, up from out of nowhere comes Andy.

1014
00:58:02.110 --> 00:58:03.650
And he's like, I agree.

1015
00:58:04.330 --> 00:58:05.750
And Michael's like, what are we?

1016
00:58:05.890 --> 00:58:06.610
How do you know?

1017
00:58:06.750 --> 00:58:07.610
What do you agree with?

1018
00:58:07.790 --> 00:58:09.450
How do you even know what we're talking about?

1019
00:58:09.870 --> 00:58:10.050
Yeah.

1020
00:58:10.210 --> 00:58:13.170
And Andy's like, Pam was like, blah, blah, something lame.

1021
00:58:14.150 --> 00:58:16.150
And then you're like, right on.

1022
00:58:17.030 --> 00:58:17.850
There it is.

1023
00:58:17.930 --> 00:58:18.530
There it is.

1024
00:58:18.790 --> 00:58:19.510
Come on.

1025
00:58:20.070 --> 00:58:20.730
Seven minutes.

1026
00:58:20.730 --> 00:58:21.830
It's 33 seconds.

1027
00:58:22.150 --> 00:58:25.530
The very first, but not the last, rid-a-da-da-doo.

1028
00:58:25.750 --> 00:58:28.530
So we're back at the party planning committee meeting.

1029
00:58:29.010 --> 00:58:30.210
Angela is sad.

1030
00:58:30.210 --> 00:58:31.390
She is sad.

1031
00:58:31.550 --> 00:58:34.070
She's not even speaking up about anything.

1032
00:58:34.270 --> 00:58:35.850
She's not even being mean to Phyllis.

1033
00:58:35.930 --> 00:58:37.330
You know the woman is sad.

1034
00:58:37.930 --> 00:58:39.110
Can I say something?

1035
00:58:39.330 --> 00:58:39.570
Yeah.

1036
00:58:40.570 --> 00:58:45.790
I think that later when we see this party, it's going to be one of the best ones we've

1037
00:58:45.790 --> 00:58:46.530
ever thrown.

1038
00:58:47.390 --> 00:58:48.970
How dare you?

1039
00:58:49.270 --> 00:58:50.610
I'm just saying.

1040
00:58:50.610 --> 00:58:54.230
I'm just saying that you're a little checked out.

1041
00:58:54.490 --> 00:58:57.090
And look what we did without you.

1042
00:58:57.290 --> 00:59:06.490
When others were allowed to participate in the planning, we threw a very, like, the decorations,

1043
00:59:07.330 --> 00:59:09.530
that Creed loved the food.

1044
00:59:09.970 --> 00:59:12.750
Let me tell you something, lady.

1045
00:59:12.970 --> 00:59:13.170
What?

1046
00:59:13.550 --> 00:59:13.890
What?

1047
00:59:14.290 --> 00:59:15.090
I...

1048
00:59:16.950 --> 00:59:18.030
am flabbergasted.

1049
00:59:20.030 --> 00:59:27.970
Well, I mean, I just want to say, I noted, I noted how disengaged from the planning Angela

1050
00:59:27.970 --> 00:59:32.130
was, and then I noticed what a really great party it was.

1051
00:59:32.310 --> 00:59:35.450
Well, you know, Michael has given the marching orders.

1052
00:59:35.590 --> 00:59:40.150
He really wants to celebrate Oscar, as Michael says, quote, his Mexican-ness.

1053
00:59:40.350 --> 00:59:42.330
He wants firecrackers, a chihuahua.

1054
00:59:42.690 --> 00:59:44.710
You know, he also tells them to get a donkey.

1055
00:59:45.190 --> 00:59:45.810
A burro.

1056
00:59:46.270 --> 00:59:53.310
Because, you know, the reason that we're throwing a Mexican-themed party is because Oscar's gayness

1057
00:59:53.310 --> 00:59:54.610
does not define him.

1058
00:59:54.770 --> 00:59:56.770
His Mexicanness is what defines him.

1059
00:59:57.630 --> 00:59:58.970
And Oscar's just like...

1060
00:59:58.970 --> 00:59:59.710
According to Michael.

1061
00:59:59.970 --> 01:00:00.370
Great.

1062
01:00:00.950 --> 01:00:01.510
Great.

1063
01:00:01.930 --> 01:00:03.290
Right back in it with Michael.

1064
01:00:03.290 --> 01:00:06.510
Oscar's thinking of all the things he's going to purchase after this party.

1065
01:00:06.690 --> 01:00:07.110
I know.

1066
01:00:08.230 --> 01:00:12.230
Well, I have a question for you about a scene coming up, Jenna.

1067
01:00:12.950 --> 01:00:13.070
Okay.

1068
01:00:13.070 --> 01:00:18.130
Was it in the script that Andy, like, fishes for Jim?

1069
01:00:18.330 --> 01:00:20.970
Like, that he throws the rod and reel and the whole thing?

1070
01:00:21.090 --> 01:00:23.470
Or was that just made up on the day?

1071
01:00:24.750 --> 01:00:26.770
Angela, I will check the script for that.

1072
01:00:26.770 --> 01:00:31.210
And in the meantime, while I'm doing that, please enjoy this whole music by Carmen and Camille

1073
01:00:31.210 --> 01:00:34.030
doing their version of Heartbreak in the Break Room.

1074
01:00:34.530 --> 01:00:35.150
One moment.

1075
01:01:03.850 --> 01:01:06.840
All right.

1076
01:01:06.980 --> 01:01:07.660
Thank you for holding.

1077
01:01:08.380 --> 01:01:10.060
I could not find that in the script.

1078
01:01:10.280 --> 01:01:11.700
It wasn't in the script.

1079
01:01:12.220 --> 01:01:12.660
No.

1080
01:01:12.660 --> 01:01:18.960
So, it was either conceived of as a rewrite page or it was something he did on the day.

1081
01:01:19.100 --> 01:01:23.600
So, what's in the script, the thing that makes Jim want to prank Andy is just more singing

1082
01:01:23.600 --> 01:01:29.400
at his desk, that he's just obnoxiously singing and then Jim decides he has to do

1083
01:01:29.400 --> 01:01:29.860
something.

1084
01:01:30.060 --> 01:01:30.400
Right.

1085
01:01:30.460 --> 01:01:33.520
But the fishing for tuna, not in the script.

1086
01:01:34.160 --> 01:01:34.400
Okay.

1087
01:01:34.400 --> 01:01:36.240
Well, it's perfect for Andy.

1088
01:01:36.360 --> 01:01:37.020
It's so perfect.

1089
01:01:37.540 --> 01:01:40.560
Jim has had it, though, and he now wants to play a prank.

1090
01:01:40.680 --> 01:01:41.340
He asked Karen.

1091
01:01:41.540 --> 01:01:42.580
Karen says she's too busy.

1092
01:01:42.660 --> 01:01:44.600
She got all of Dwight's clients.

1093
01:01:45.000 --> 01:01:50.420
Then he asked Ryan, and lady, we have some Ryan sass.

1094
01:01:50.740 --> 01:01:51.680
I loved it.

1095
01:01:52.380 --> 01:01:53.680
I'm falling in love with Ryan.

1096
01:01:53.840 --> 01:01:54.500
I know you are.

1097
01:01:54.620 --> 01:01:55.180
Not going to lie.

1098
01:01:55.240 --> 01:01:55.800
I know you are.

1099
01:01:55.960 --> 01:01:56.860
What does he say?

1100
01:01:57.500 --> 01:01:58.640
I'll tell you what he said.

1101
01:01:58.800 --> 01:02:00.320
He says, oh, you know what?

1102
01:02:00.420 --> 01:02:02.940
Not right now, but ask me again 10 years ago.

1103
01:02:02.940 --> 01:02:12.280
Oh, and I feel like John's, the look on John's face as Jim in that moment is so good.

1104
01:02:12.740 --> 01:02:13.480
So good.

1105
01:02:13.600 --> 01:02:14.440
He's like, all right, man.

1106
01:02:14.440 --> 01:02:16.100
I liked you better when you were the temp.

1107
01:02:16.680 --> 01:02:17.620
Ryan's like, so did I.

1108
01:02:17.820 --> 01:02:18.660
Ryan says, so did I.

1109
01:02:19.100 --> 01:02:20.920
That's some serious Ryan sass.

1110
01:02:21.280 --> 01:02:23.400
So, Angela, should we check in with Dwight now?

1111
01:02:23.880 --> 01:02:25.920
See how he's doing over at Staples?

1112
01:02:26.620 --> 01:02:27.020
Yes.

1113
01:02:27.500 --> 01:02:28.600
He's doing great.

1114
01:02:28.780 --> 01:02:29.600
He's crushing it.

1115
01:02:29.820 --> 01:02:30.620
He is.

1116
01:02:30.780 --> 01:02:37.160
We had some fan questions about Staples from Amy Jackson, Aaron Westra, Ainsley Thompson,

1117
01:02:37.460 --> 01:02:41.140
Jeff Needham, Diamond P, and Kate N.

1118
01:02:41.360 --> 01:02:45.820
They wanted to know, did we film in an actual Staples store?

1119
01:02:47.540 --> 01:02:47.980
Yes.

1120
01:02:48.300 --> 01:02:49.180
Yes, we did.

1121
01:02:49.640 --> 01:02:51.680
We filmed at a real Staples.

1122
01:02:51.900 --> 01:02:54.020
It was at the Empire Center in Burbank.

1123
01:02:55.140 --> 01:03:00.540
I've actually been there many times, not only to the Empire Center, but to this actual Staples.

1124
01:03:00.720 --> 01:03:03.840
I have purchased my home printer at this Staples.

1125
01:03:04.480 --> 01:03:08.560
Jenna, I feel like we went there for like a BFF afternoon where we went to Target and then

1126
01:03:08.560 --> 01:03:09.540
we went to Staples together.

1127
01:03:09.720 --> 01:03:10.820
I have like a memory of that.

1128
01:03:11.460 --> 01:03:12.140
Oh, yeah.

1129
01:03:12.140 --> 01:03:16.180
I'm sure we did that because then there's that donut place that you like.

1130
01:03:16.380 --> 01:03:16.780
What is it?

1131
01:03:16.920 --> 01:03:17.540
Krispy Kreme.

1132
01:03:17.660 --> 01:03:18.320
Krispy Kreme.

1133
01:03:18.420 --> 01:03:19.480
What's not to like?

1134
01:03:19.960 --> 01:03:20.320
Exactly.

1135
01:03:20.500 --> 01:03:21.540
And they have a drive-thru.

1136
01:03:21.700 --> 01:03:22.840
They have a drive-thru.

1137
01:03:23.400 --> 01:03:27.260
They have a drive-thru and they also have this conveyor belt that you can watch.

1138
01:03:27.400 --> 01:03:30.720
It's like watching a car wash, but it's donuts going by.

1139
01:03:31.000 --> 01:03:35.180
And then you get to the end and they just take it right off the conveyor belt and it's

1140
01:03:35.180 --> 01:03:38.340
super warm and they hand it to you and kids love it.

1141
01:03:38.560 --> 01:03:40.800
It's like a mini donut factory.

1142
01:03:41.800 --> 01:03:43.480
Well, I would take my kids there all the time.

1143
01:03:43.600 --> 01:03:46.440
I think that the first time we went, you and I didn't even have kids.

1144
01:03:47.720 --> 01:03:48.640
Well, this is true.

1145
01:03:48.780 --> 01:03:49.340
This is true.

1146
01:03:49.720 --> 01:03:49.920
Okay.

1147
01:03:50.220 --> 01:03:51.920
So, yeah, Dwight is crushing it.

1148
01:03:52.040 --> 01:03:53.780
Sorry, we got off on a tangent about donuts.

1149
01:03:54.080 --> 01:03:54.380
Go figure.

1150
01:03:54.700 --> 01:03:54.880
We did.

1151
01:03:55.220 --> 01:03:59.620
But I want to say, remember back in the merger when we talked about how Staples paid

1152
01:03:59.620 --> 01:04:06.140
the production to feature one of its shredders in an episode, people were asking if this was

1153
01:04:06.140 --> 01:04:08.560
still part of that product integration.

1154
01:04:09.380 --> 01:04:09.900
No.

1155
01:04:10.420 --> 01:04:10.800
No.

1156
01:04:10.960 --> 01:04:12.440
This was just a plot point.

1157
01:04:12.580 --> 01:04:16.580
They just thought it would be funny that Dwight ends up going to work for Dunder Mifflin's

1158
01:04:16.580 --> 01:04:17.060
competitor.

1159
01:04:17.460 --> 01:04:21.380
So, Staples did not pay to be featured in this episode at all.

1160
01:04:21.380 --> 01:04:23.600
And then, guess what they did?

1161
01:04:23.900 --> 01:04:24.060
What?

1162
01:04:24.540 --> 01:04:26.860
They did something insane to the Staples.

1163
01:04:27.120 --> 01:04:27.580
What did they do?

1164
01:04:27.580 --> 01:04:29.620
So, I'm going to let Greg tell you.

1165
01:04:29.620 --> 01:04:39.420
We arranged to have a real Staples be the location for this episode, and I had scouted

1166
01:04:39.420 --> 01:04:39.700
it.

1167
01:04:40.200 --> 01:04:47.540
And then, between the time that I scouted it and the time that we showed up to shoot, they

1168
01:04:47.540 --> 01:04:53.660
had replaced all the Staples signage with very unrealistic-looking Staples signs that

1169
01:04:53.660 --> 01:04:58.600
were three times bigger than what we had seen because they wanted more of an advertising

1170
01:04:58.600 --> 01:05:04.140
pop in the background of our show in the morning of the day we were supposed to shoot there.

1171
01:05:04.340 --> 01:05:09.660
And so, it became like a thing about, you know, we had to make our day and we had to

1172
01:05:09.660 --> 01:05:13.320
shoot, but I didn't want to turn the show into an ad for Staples.

1173
01:05:13.500 --> 01:05:16.200
So, there was a lot of shooting around it.

1174
01:05:16.280 --> 01:05:21.960
And I believe the last shot where the camera kind of zooms into a security camera to see

1175
01:05:21.960 --> 01:05:28.180
them exiting was to avoid a gigantic Staples sign that they had put up at the last minute.

1176
01:05:28.960 --> 01:05:33.120
Ooh, Staples.

1177
01:05:33.240 --> 01:05:33.920
Can you blame them?

1178
01:05:33.980 --> 01:05:35.500
They're like, hey, we got a camera crew here.

1179
01:05:35.600 --> 01:05:36.600
I'm going to put up my big sign.

1180
01:05:37.060 --> 01:05:38.480
I'd probably do the same thing.

1181
01:05:38.640 --> 01:05:39.560
I would do the same thing.

1182
01:05:39.960 --> 01:05:42.540
They were like, Henry, get over here.

1183
01:05:42.740 --> 01:05:45.040
Bring the tall ladder and the big signs.

1184
01:05:45.300 --> 01:05:45.560
Yeah.

1185
01:05:46.040 --> 01:05:46.960
Get it on TV.

1186
01:05:47.980 --> 01:05:51.420
You know I love the Staples folks because they give back to teachers, Jenna.

1187
01:05:51.640 --> 01:05:53.580
So, oh, yeah.

1188
01:05:53.880 --> 01:05:54.500
I love them.

1189
01:05:54.620 --> 01:05:55.800
But that is very funny.

1190
01:05:56.020 --> 01:05:59.300
I have a little piece of trivia, though, about that day.

1191
01:05:59.300 --> 01:06:07.040
Dave Rogers said that Greg got really sick that day, so sick that he had to go home halfway

1192
01:06:07.040 --> 01:06:09.160
through the day and Randall took over.

1193
01:06:09.940 --> 01:06:10.680
Whoa.

1194
01:06:11.040 --> 01:06:11.400
Yeah.

1195
01:06:11.800 --> 01:06:13.140
That's crazy.

1196
01:06:13.420 --> 01:06:13.940
I know.

1197
01:06:15.320 --> 01:06:20.400
Well, listen, I want to talk a little bit about Dwight's new co-worker, Paris.

1198
01:06:20.620 --> 01:06:21.440
She's amazing.

1199
01:06:21.860 --> 01:06:27.480
Played by Yvette Nicole Brown, who would later go to star in Community.

1200
01:06:27.480 --> 01:06:28.360
Mm-hmm.

1201
01:06:28.680 --> 01:06:33.400
This scene with them in the break room eating lunch, I watched it three times.

1202
01:06:33.800 --> 01:06:37.500
I watched it three times because she is so funny.

1203
01:06:38.240 --> 01:06:40.540
Her, like, you know what it is?

1204
01:06:40.660 --> 01:06:46.360
I feel like we're getting this opportunity to have someone outside of the Dunder Mifflin

1205
01:06:46.360 --> 01:06:48.960
family react to Dwight Schrute.

1206
01:06:49.260 --> 01:06:51.480
We all know what Dwight is like.

1207
01:06:51.480 --> 01:06:52.960
We know what to expect from him.

1208
01:06:53.140 --> 01:07:00.220
So to place Dwight in the real world with a regular person who's not used to him was so

1209
01:07:00.220 --> 01:07:00.980
funny to me.

1210
01:07:01.160 --> 01:07:07.400
And her reactions were what I would imagine anyone would react like if they met Dwight.

1211
01:07:07.840 --> 01:07:08.160
Yes.

1212
01:07:08.180 --> 01:07:09.480
I texted her.

1213
01:07:09.680 --> 01:07:16.240
I said, Yvette, I just want you to know I forgot about this scene and how great it was

1214
01:07:16.240 --> 01:07:17.320
and re-watching it.

1215
01:07:17.420 --> 01:07:17.980
It was hilarious.

1216
01:07:18.220 --> 01:07:21.780
And she was like, oh, Angela, I feel like I was just there for a blip.

1217
01:07:21.880 --> 01:07:24.160
And I said, Yvette, you stole the scene.

1218
01:07:24.280 --> 01:07:25.660
You stole the scene.

1219
01:07:26.200 --> 01:07:26.440
Yes.

1220
01:07:26.960 --> 01:07:30.560
Now, you mentioned, Angela, that you were watching this episode with your kids.

1221
01:07:30.780 --> 01:07:34.760
My son walked into my office while I was watching this scene.

1222
01:07:34.880 --> 01:07:36.000
He was laughing.

1223
01:07:36.080 --> 01:07:43.700
And then he and I looked for a fan catch that was sent in by Lori Lex.

1224
01:07:43.960 --> 01:07:45.280
Oh, what'd you guys find?

1225
01:07:46.240 --> 01:07:46.760
Oh, my gosh.

1226
01:07:46.900 --> 01:07:52.100
My son was so tickled because during this scene, Dwight's sandwich that he's eating

1227
01:07:52.100 --> 01:07:55.180
gets bigger rather than smaller as he eats it.

1228
01:07:56.900 --> 01:07:59.000
Because they use different takes.

1229
01:07:59.400 --> 01:08:05.360
So at 12 minutes, 21 seconds, all that's left is like a little corner of bread.

1230
01:08:05.520 --> 01:08:09.020
And then at 12 minutes, 28 seconds, it's much larger.

1231
01:08:09.300 --> 01:08:10.100
I love it.

1232
01:08:10.240 --> 01:08:13.520
I love how into this episode our kids were with background catches.

1233
01:08:13.900 --> 01:08:14.520
I know.

1234
01:08:15.000 --> 01:08:15.980
It's so cute.

1235
01:08:16.660 --> 01:08:19.940
Well, lady, I want to talk about the scene with Michael and Angela.

1236
01:08:20.740 --> 01:08:22.420
They're in the break room.

1237
01:08:22.980 --> 01:08:25.820
And they're clearly both missing Dwight.

1238
01:08:26.040 --> 01:08:29.780
But obviously, neither of them are saying that to each other.

1239
01:08:30.060 --> 01:08:33.660
And Michael just says, Oh, it's good to have Oscar back.

1240
01:08:34.000 --> 01:08:35.140
And Angela's like, Yeah.

1241
01:08:35.140 --> 01:08:39.660
And they both just sort of sadly take a sip of their beverage and look off into space.

1242
01:08:40.120 --> 01:08:46.340
And I never, ever got quiet moment scenes with Steve.

1243
01:08:46.700 --> 01:08:53.660
And so in rewatching this, it was so special to me because I just, our characters hardly ever interacted.

1244
01:08:53.660 --> 01:08:56.420
And when they did, I was usually mad at him, you know?

1245
01:08:56.860 --> 01:08:57.140
Yeah.

1246
01:08:57.320 --> 01:08:58.540
So that was really special.

1247
01:08:58.540 --> 01:09:09.500
And then on a total tangent, there is a fantastic shot at 13 minutes, 47 seconds of Luanne's water fountain.

1248
01:09:09.500 --> 01:09:11.800
And it's there like gurgling away.

1249
01:09:12.780 --> 01:09:15.540
Lady, I saw the same thing.

1250
01:09:15.540 --> 01:09:17.360
I saw the same thing.

1251
01:09:17.700 --> 01:09:23.660
I think that's what was in the background of that kitchen scene in that other episode that we all thought was a fireplace.

1252
01:09:24.040 --> 01:09:26.360
I think it was Luanne's water feature.

1253
01:09:26.640 --> 01:09:29.580
She had a Zen garden and a water fountain.

1254
01:09:29.860 --> 01:09:30.380
She did.

1255
01:09:30.520 --> 01:09:32.480
And they never plugged it in because it made noise.

1256
01:09:32.640 --> 01:09:35.860
But every once in a while, I guess, it got plugged in.

1257
01:09:35.860 --> 01:09:43.620
And I think you're right because it has a little blue light in it that maybe we thought was a fire something.

1258
01:09:44.120 --> 01:09:44.520
Yes.

1259
01:09:45.240 --> 01:09:45.880
Oh, my God.

1260
01:09:45.880 --> 01:09:48.360
I love that we both got excited about Luanne's fountain.

1261
01:09:49.060 --> 01:09:57.020
Well, Jenna, I think on that note of getting super excited about a fountain in the background, we should take a break.

1262
01:09:57.880 --> 01:10:01.240
Yeah, we'll take a break and then we'll come back and get into this big prank.

1263
01:10:05.940 --> 01:10:07.780
All right, guys, we are back.

1264
01:10:08.240 --> 01:10:09.520
Angela, do you know what I'm doing right now?

1265
01:10:10.280 --> 01:10:10.900
No.

1266
01:10:11.240 --> 01:10:12.880
I mean, I can see you, but.

1267
01:10:13.220 --> 01:10:14.400
I'm making bread.

1268
01:10:14.620 --> 01:10:17.740
I can't see your hands, but I know your left one is moving.

1269
01:10:18.200 --> 01:10:21.600
No, I'm not literally making bread in my lap.

1270
01:10:23.220 --> 01:10:29.560
I'm sitting here podcasting, but I am simultaneously bread making.

1271
01:10:29.560 --> 01:10:39.440
Like, that's the cool thing about bread making is that I have dough that is rising into a little living dough baby that I'm going to put in my oven and turn into crisp,

1272
01:10:39.540 --> 01:10:40.640
delicious sourdough bread.

1273
01:10:40.640 --> 01:10:45.200
As we speak, that science is working in my kitchen on my counter right now.

1274
01:10:45.200 --> 01:10:47.980
During this break, I molded my little dough baby.

1275
01:10:48.780 --> 01:10:49.340
Aw.

1276
01:10:49.720 --> 01:10:50.040
Yeah.

1277
01:10:50.220 --> 01:10:52.620
Well, I molded another dough baby.

1278
01:10:52.900 --> 01:10:58.840
I like to call my belly because I went downstairs and ate a little piece of this.

1279
01:10:58.840 --> 01:11:01.120
I don't even know what it is that Josh made.

1280
01:11:01.280 --> 01:11:04.800
It's like some kind of it tastes like a little square of pecan pie.

1281
01:11:05.060 --> 01:11:05.740
It's so good.

1282
01:11:05.740 --> 01:11:09.840
Can we give a plug to Josh's baking page, please?

1283
01:11:10.180 --> 01:11:14.560
Baking with Josh and Ange, there is a recipe on there for something called a brookie.

1284
01:11:15.320 --> 01:11:15.960
Mm-hmm.

1285
01:11:16.180 --> 01:11:16.460
Okay.

1286
01:11:16.760 --> 01:11:18.700
You know, I made this the other day.

1287
01:11:18.920 --> 01:11:25.380
It is a layer of brownie topped with a layer of chocolate chip cookie and their bars.

1288
01:11:26.340 --> 01:11:30.560
Angela, I ate so many of them that I made myself sick.

1289
01:11:30.560 --> 01:11:37.000
I made myself sick like I was like a child who couldn't stop eating candy on Halloween.

1290
01:11:37.460 --> 01:11:39.720
And I felt so ill.

1291
01:11:39.880 --> 01:11:45.980
And even when I felt sick from eating so many of them, I wanted to eat more of them.

1292
01:11:46.100 --> 01:11:47.760
That's how good the brookie is, guys.

1293
01:11:47.920 --> 01:11:51.200
It'll make you sick and you won't care and you'll keep eating it anyway.

1294
01:11:51.460 --> 01:11:55.980
I don't know what kind of endorsement that is, but I feel like that's a good endorsement.

1295
01:11:57.100 --> 01:11:57.580
Yeah.

1296
01:11:57.760 --> 01:11:59.600
Well, he has tons of recipes, you guys.

1297
01:11:59.600 --> 01:12:00.580
My husband is a baker.

1298
01:12:00.880 --> 01:12:04.680
You can go to bakingwithjoshandange.com for all of his recipes.

1299
01:12:04.960 --> 01:12:07.600
I don't even know why I'm in the equation there.

1300
01:12:07.820 --> 01:12:10.200
It's just that when he bakes, he likes me around.

1301
01:12:11.580 --> 01:12:13.080
But he is the master.

1302
01:12:13.340 --> 01:12:15.760
I'm the taste tester and he's the master.

1303
01:12:16.000 --> 01:12:17.440
That was really sweet, Jenna.

1304
01:12:17.580 --> 01:12:22.040
Well, if you want to eat so much of something that you make yourself sick, make the brookie.

1305
01:12:22.280 --> 01:12:24.920
But he also has, guys, not just sweets.

1306
01:12:24.920 --> 01:12:27.740
He's got, like, these one-sheet meals.

1307
01:12:28.320 --> 01:12:32.360
And I love to cook things on one sheet because then I only have to clean one thing.

1308
01:12:32.960 --> 01:12:34.080
Yes, they are really good.

1309
01:12:34.080 --> 01:12:36.220
We just did his one-sheet chicken fajitas.

1310
01:12:36.460 --> 01:12:37.080
That's my favorite.

1311
01:12:37.700 --> 01:12:38.660
It's so good.

1312
01:12:39.000 --> 01:12:39.280
All right.

1313
01:12:39.400 --> 01:12:43.720
This became a small commercial for bakingwithjoshandange.com, but I stand by it.

1314
01:12:44.740 --> 01:12:45.560
Well, thanks.

1315
01:12:45.720 --> 01:12:46.700
That's really sweet.

1316
01:12:46.700 --> 01:12:47.320
I'll tell him.

1317
01:12:47.440 --> 01:12:48.020
He'll be tickled.

1318
01:12:48.740 --> 01:12:49.320
All right.

1319
01:12:49.460 --> 01:12:51.120
Well, let's get back to this episode.

1320
01:12:52.540 --> 01:12:54.780
Jim steals Andy's cell phone.

1321
01:12:55.020 --> 01:12:55.160
Yeah.

1322
01:12:55.340 --> 01:12:57.380
But why does he pass it off to Pam?

1323
01:12:57.520 --> 01:12:59.640
I don't understand why they trade it twice.

1324
01:13:00.240 --> 01:13:01.560
What are they, secret spies?

1325
01:13:01.820 --> 01:13:06.540
Couldn't he have just taken it and gone straight to the bathroom and, like, chucked it up in

1326
01:13:06.540 --> 01:13:07.780
the ceiling or something?

1327
01:13:07.960 --> 01:13:08.280
Yes.

1328
01:13:08.380 --> 01:13:10.920
This entire prank could have been done by Jim alone.

1329
01:13:10.920 --> 01:13:17.740
He tried to recruit all these people to do this prank with him that required only one

1330
01:13:17.740 --> 01:13:18.160
person.

1331
01:13:18.340 --> 01:13:24.260
He could have pranked Andy on his own, but for Jim, the prank is like the social bonding

1332
01:13:24.260 --> 01:13:24.800
experience.

1333
01:13:24.800 --> 01:13:28.060
It's not about, like, just doing it by himself.

1334
01:13:28.540 --> 01:13:29.660
What's the fun in that?

1335
01:13:29.740 --> 01:13:30.060
Exactly.

1336
01:13:30.580 --> 01:13:30.860
He wants a partner.

1337
01:13:31.020 --> 01:13:31.700
He wants a buddy.

1338
01:13:31.880 --> 01:13:32.240
Yes.

1339
01:13:33.100 --> 01:13:37.980
So he does this weird thing where he knocks over the pens and steals the phone and then

1340
01:13:37.980 --> 01:13:41.240
gives it to Pam and then Pam gives it back to him.

1341
01:13:41.860 --> 01:13:43.640
And Karen clocks it.

1342
01:13:43.760 --> 01:13:43.960
Yeah.

1343
01:13:44.180 --> 01:13:44.780
Karen notices.

1344
01:13:45.100 --> 01:13:48.140
She doesn't know what they're doing, but they're in cahoots.

1345
01:13:48.320 --> 01:13:48.720
Well.

1346
01:13:48.860 --> 01:13:53.100
And then you're like his lookout, but you can clearly see him.

1347
01:13:53.320 --> 01:13:58.240
You guys have the most, like, you're the most oddball, like, duo.

1348
01:13:58.660 --> 01:14:03.280
I feel like there could have been a spinoff where Jim and Pam are secret spies, but everyone

1349
01:14:03.280 --> 01:14:03.660
knows.

1350
01:14:03.660 --> 01:14:10.700
Well, and just to our point earlier, is no one noticing the camera crew following Jim

1351
01:14:10.700 --> 01:14:14.560
and Pam sneaking and, like, filming them do this prank?

1352
01:14:14.740 --> 01:14:19.280
There's a lot of disbelief you have to suspend right here in this moment.

1353
01:14:19.500 --> 01:14:24.440
Jenna, no one sees it because Pam is so great at distracting them by drinking her water.

1354
01:14:27.700 --> 01:14:29.020
That's all we see.

1355
01:14:29.180 --> 01:14:31.300
Pam's just drinking her water and playing with her necklace.

1356
01:14:31.620 --> 01:14:32.520
Nothing to see here.

1357
01:14:32.620 --> 01:14:32.860
Yeah.

1358
01:14:33.280 --> 01:14:34.200
What do you mean?

1359
01:14:34.360 --> 01:14:34.620
What?

1360
01:14:34.620 --> 01:14:40.460
Well, you have to remember, in the last episode, Phyllis kind of spills the beans and says to

1361
01:14:40.460 --> 01:14:46.580
Karen, I'm so glad you and Jim are together because he was hung up on Pam for so long.

1362
01:14:46.760 --> 01:14:49.620
So, you know, Karen has got that in her brain.

1363
01:14:49.620 --> 01:14:53.880
And when she sees the two of them kind of giggling and up to something, she's like,

1364
01:14:53.960 --> 01:14:55.060
oh, no, what's happening?

1365
01:14:55.520 --> 01:14:55.740
Yes.

1366
01:14:56.140 --> 01:14:59.260
Well, meanwhile, Kelly and Oscar are setting up for the party.

1367
01:14:59.440 --> 01:15:02.200
I think it's very funny that Oscar has to set up his own party.

1368
01:15:02.300 --> 01:15:03.960
He has chores at his own party.

1369
01:15:04.960 --> 01:15:05.600
It's amazing.

1370
01:15:06.120 --> 01:15:08.940
And then Michael, meanwhile, is pouting in the kitchen.

1371
01:15:09.360 --> 01:15:11.440
He wants to let Jim know that he's not fine.

1372
01:15:12.180 --> 01:15:13.060
He's not fine.

1373
01:15:13.380 --> 01:15:15.060
And he's like, he doesn't want to talk about it.

1374
01:15:15.160 --> 01:15:15.900
But Jim's like, OK.

1375
01:15:16.040 --> 01:15:17.320
And he's like, OK, I'll talk about it.

1376
01:15:17.380 --> 01:15:18.000
He's like, OK.

1377
01:15:18.220 --> 01:15:18.460
Yeah.

1378
01:15:18.860 --> 01:15:20.640
And he's like, what do you think of Andy?

1379
01:15:21.140 --> 01:15:22.180
What do you think of Andy?

1380
01:15:22.520 --> 01:15:24.100
And I love this, Angela.

1381
01:15:24.360 --> 01:15:26.580
Jim is like, well, I mean, he's kind of a yes man.

1382
01:15:26.580 --> 01:15:28.540
And Michael's like, that's not true.

1383
01:15:28.540 --> 01:15:31.800
Because when I say I don't like something, he says he doesn't like it, too.

1384
01:15:32.960 --> 01:15:34.080
It's like, oh, Michael.

1385
01:15:34.760 --> 01:15:35.220
Oh, Michael.

1386
01:15:35.700 --> 01:15:37.760
Steve is so brilliant in this episode.

1387
01:15:37.760 --> 01:15:42.340
I know we talk about how good he is so, like, every week.

1388
01:15:42.640 --> 01:15:48.740
But he had to, I don't even know how to say it.

1389
01:15:48.840 --> 01:15:56.380
But the way he reacts to Andy is like a whole new version of Michael Scott we haven't seen.

1390
01:15:56.380 --> 01:15:58.280
And he's so brilliant.

1391
01:15:58.600 --> 01:16:04.660
And the way he doesn't get things and then the audience gets it before him and then he finally gets it.

1392
01:16:04.740 --> 01:16:05.960
It's just amazing.

1393
01:16:06.440 --> 01:16:13.880
Well, Angela, he has this talking head that I can't even barely watch because...

1394
01:16:13.880 --> 01:16:15.020
Is it about the raspberry?

1395
01:16:15.240 --> 01:16:15.540
Yeah.

1396
01:16:15.720 --> 01:16:16.640
The sherbet thing?

1397
01:16:16.800 --> 01:16:20.320
It's about the way Steve delivers it is so masterful.

1398
01:16:20.440 --> 01:16:23.520
But the whole thing just makes me so uncomfortable.

1399
01:16:24.380 --> 01:16:28.180
Whenever Michael talks about his childhood, I get scared.

1400
01:16:28.920 --> 01:16:40.000
I just feel like I don't want more details about his loneliness and his, like, need for attention and his, all of it.

1401
01:16:40.280 --> 01:16:43.380
His awkward interactions with his mom and stepdad, Jeff.

1402
01:16:43.700 --> 01:16:44.300
I mean...

1403
01:16:44.300 --> 01:16:44.580
Yeah.

1404
01:16:45.180 --> 01:16:45.680
Yeah.

1405
01:16:46.120 --> 01:16:46.960
I know.

1406
01:16:47.220 --> 01:16:48.020
Poor Michael.

1407
01:16:48.020 --> 01:16:53.380
I know this is totally off topic, but I was impressed that Jim's choice of snack was raw carrot.

1408
01:16:54.460 --> 01:16:55.020
Yes!

1409
01:16:55.420 --> 01:16:55.960
Angela!

1410
01:16:56.600 --> 01:16:58.000
Angela, we had...

1411
01:16:58.000 --> 01:17:01.180
We had a fan point this out about the carrots.

1412
01:17:01.740 --> 01:17:03.600
Brianna Kernan wrote in to say,

1413
01:17:03.780 --> 01:17:06.060
Does John really like to snack on carrots?

1414
01:17:06.060 --> 01:17:11.220
Because he can be seen in multiple episodes snacking on carrots at various times.

1415
01:17:11.660 --> 01:17:13.540
I did a lot of scenes with John.

1416
01:17:13.740 --> 01:17:16.480
And so I can tell you that he eats carrots.

1417
01:17:16.480 --> 01:17:22.360
If given the choice for what he gets to eat in a scene, he will pick something healthy.

1418
01:17:22.560 --> 01:17:24.980
He will pick carrots a lot.

1419
01:17:25.160 --> 01:17:25.840
He would pick carrots.

1420
01:17:25.960 --> 01:17:31.280
To the point that they finally had to say, John, you can't with the carrots.

1421
01:17:31.280 --> 01:17:32.960
It's, like, really bad for sound.

1422
01:17:32.980 --> 01:17:35.160
So then he started eating grapes.

1423
01:17:36.300 --> 01:17:37.080
Oh, wow.

1424
01:17:37.080 --> 01:17:38.600
So you'll see him eat some grapes.

1425
01:17:38.640 --> 01:17:41.960
But occasionally it would be scripted that we're eating chips.

1426
01:17:42.720 --> 01:17:43.320
Mm-hmm.

1427
01:17:43.600 --> 01:17:47.460
And he would eat the chips, but he preferred a healthy snack, guys.

1428
01:17:47.760 --> 01:17:48.480
He just did.

1429
01:17:49.620 --> 01:17:51.400
I am very impressed, John.

1430
01:17:51.600 --> 01:17:52.480
I'm very impressed.

1431
01:17:53.640 --> 01:17:56.720
I mean, I usually would ask for potato chips.

1432
01:17:57.600 --> 01:17:57.940
Yeah.

1433
01:17:58.380 --> 01:17:58.940
Well, B.J.

1434
01:17:59.040 --> 01:18:02.220
Novak and I used to say that if it's a prop, it doesn't have any calories,

1435
01:18:02.220 --> 01:18:04.160
so you can eat as much of it as you want.

1436
01:18:04.680 --> 01:18:06.040
Oh, interesting theory.

1437
01:18:06.220 --> 01:18:06.340
Yeah.

1438
01:18:06.400 --> 01:18:07.220
It's not real food.

1439
01:18:07.360 --> 01:18:07.860
You're pretending.

1440
01:18:08.540 --> 01:18:09.380
It's pretend food.

1441
01:18:09.520 --> 01:18:09.760
It's pretend food.

1442
01:18:09.760 --> 01:18:10.180
No calories.

1443
01:18:10.460 --> 01:18:11.260
Pretend calories.

1444
01:18:11.400 --> 01:18:13.440
You know what I would pick now is a brookie.

1445
01:18:14.040 --> 01:18:16.440
I'd be like, can I snack on a brookie, please?

1446
01:18:16.900 --> 01:18:22.200
Well, the party setup is underway, but Angela and Pam have a little conversation out by the

1447
01:18:22.200 --> 01:18:28.400
elevators, and I loved it so much, Jenna, when Pam's like, is it about Dwight?

1448
01:18:28.680 --> 01:18:30.860
And Angela's like, no, John Denver.

1449
01:18:31.580 --> 01:18:34.180
You're like, okay, that's how it's going to be.

1450
01:18:34.340 --> 01:18:34.740
I'm out.

1451
01:18:34.880 --> 01:18:35.040
Yeah.

1452
01:18:35.180 --> 01:18:35.920
No, no, no, no, no.

1453
01:18:36.340 --> 01:18:39.980
But is John Denver like one of her favorite singers?

1454
01:18:40.180 --> 01:18:41.700
Like, where did John Denver come from?

1455
01:18:41.840 --> 01:18:46.120
It's just such a funny sort of little bit of detail to me about Angela Martin.

1456
01:18:46.540 --> 01:18:50.420
Well, Angela tells Pam that she's really missing Dwight, and she feels bad.

1457
01:18:50.560 --> 01:18:50.800
Yeah.

1458
01:18:50.800 --> 01:18:53.560
And Pam says, I think you should talk to Michael.

1459
01:18:54.960 --> 01:19:00.560
And Angela's like, Pam, I'm not like you walking around in your provocative outfits saying whatever

1460
01:19:00.560 --> 01:19:02.080
thought pops in your head.

1461
01:19:02.520 --> 01:19:03.080
Yeah.

1462
01:19:04.160 --> 01:19:04.920
I love that.

1463
01:19:04.920 --> 01:19:11.800
As she's wearing a sweater over a button down, like, what are these outfits, Angela?

1464
01:19:11.960 --> 01:19:13.320
What are you even talking about?

1465
01:19:13.560 --> 01:19:13.840
Yes.

1466
01:19:13.840 --> 01:19:20.160
But anyway, Angela appreciates Pam's, you know, talking with her and gives her such a weird hug.

1467
01:19:20.340 --> 01:19:24.640
It's like she hugs her, and then when she realizes she's hugging you, she shoves you away.

1468
01:19:24.860 --> 01:19:26.840
Well, we had a fan question about it, Angela.

1469
01:19:27.040 --> 01:19:33.780
Caleb Feener and Kylie Campbell both ask, was that hug improvised or was it in the script?

1470
01:19:35.560 --> 01:19:36.700
What do you think, Angela?

1471
01:19:37.300 --> 01:19:37.700
Well.

1472
01:19:37.900 --> 01:19:38.980
Improvised or in the script?

1473
01:19:39.500 --> 01:19:41.400
I feel like it was improvised.

1474
01:19:41.700 --> 01:19:43.660
It was improvised.

1475
01:19:44.180 --> 01:19:45.460
It was not in the script.

1476
01:19:45.920 --> 01:19:47.100
It was not in the script.

1477
01:19:47.100 --> 01:19:48.100
That was improvised.

1478
01:19:48.900 --> 01:19:49.400
Yeah, yeah.

1479
01:19:49.460 --> 01:19:52.060
I feel like you and I played around with that scene a few different ways.

1480
01:19:52.060 --> 01:19:53.180
It was so fun.

1481
01:19:53.300 --> 01:19:53.880
That was great.

1482
01:19:54.080 --> 01:19:54.920
That was great.

1483
01:19:54.920 --> 01:20:01.300
Well, back in the bullpen, Jim just keeps calling Andy's phone, which is ringing now up in the ceiling.

1484
01:20:01.700 --> 01:20:07.500
And a lot of people asked, was the phone really in the ceiling playing the song?

1485
01:20:07.840 --> 01:20:16.500
Now, normally, I feel like the answer would be no, because it would ruin your ability to edit the scene.

1486
01:20:17.220 --> 01:20:22.640
But Angela, I remember that phone playing up in the ceiling.

1487
01:20:22.920 --> 01:20:23.960
Am I going crazy?

1488
01:20:25.240 --> 01:20:27.260
No, I feel like I remember it, too.

1489
01:20:27.800 --> 01:20:33.980
I feel like they put a speaker up in the ceiling and they had someone play that song for us to react to.

1490
01:20:34.420 --> 01:20:38.220
I have, like, such a strong memory of hearing it all day long.

1491
01:20:38.680 --> 01:20:40.060
Like, over our heads.

1492
01:20:40.120 --> 01:20:40.500
Yes.

1493
01:20:40.620 --> 01:20:40.840
Yeah.

1494
01:20:41.060 --> 01:20:41.360
Yes.

1495
01:20:41.440 --> 01:20:41.680
Yeah.

1496
01:20:41.960 --> 01:20:42.840
I do, too.

1497
01:20:43.000 --> 01:20:44.460
So, guys, no one can remember.

1498
01:20:44.460 --> 01:20:46.660
I reached out to a bunch of people about this.

1499
01:20:46.940 --> 01:20:47.820
What's the deal?

1500
01:20:48.320 --> 01:20:49.360
No one is sure.

1501
01:20:49.360 --> 01:20:53.780
But I'm going with my personal memory that we really did have.

1502
01:20:53.940 --> 01:20:59.520
I don't know if it was the phone, but we really were listening to that four-part harmony up in the ceiling and reacting to it.

1503
01:21:00.080 --> 01:21:00.480
Yeah.

1504
01:21:00.560 --> 01:21:01.780
We weren't reacting to nothing.

1505
01:21:02.420 --> 01:21:04.300
It was actually getting really annoying.

1506
01:21:04.540 --> 01:21:04.940
It was.

1507
01:21:04.940 --> 01:21:05.820
I do remember that.

1508
01:21:05.980 --> 01:21:07.120
I was, like, so sick of that song.

1509
01:21:07.240 --> 01:21:07.600
That's what.

1510
01:21:07.600 --> 01:21:08.340
I was like, oh, my God.

1511
01:21:09.180 --> 01:21:16.220
Angela, when we were re-watching this episode and it played for the first time, I kind of, like, I recoiled a little bit.

1512
01:21:16.380 --> 01:21:18.860
Like, the cells in my body were like, oh, no, not again.

1513
01:21:19.540 --> 01:21:20.220
Not again.

1514
01:21:20.340 --> 01:21:20.960
You're like, since memory.

1515
01:21:21.220 --> 01:21:21.660
Yes.

1516
01:21:21.800 --> 01:21:25.680
Because I remember shooting this episode and singing it.

1517
01:21:25.680 --> 01:21:35.320
And then when I went to bed the night I re-watched it, I was like, up in the two times all a day long, rocking in the bed when I sing a new song.

1518
01:21:35.520 --> 01:21:36.840
I couldn't.

1519
01:21:37.380 --> 01:21:39.360
I was like, don't do this to me again.

1520
01:21:39.500 --> 01:21:44.080
We cannot skip past what I like to call nimble Phyllis.

1521
01:21:45.240 --> 01:21:45.720
Yes.

1522
01:21:47.280 --> 01:21:48.480
She's so nimble.

1523
01:21:48.680 --> 01:21:49.760
She's agile.

1524
01:21:49.980 --> 01:21:50.960
She's quick.

1525
01:21:51.300 --> 01:21:53.600
I mean, Andy tries to open her drawer.

1526
01:21:53.960 --> 01:21:55.540
Phyllis does the no look.

1527
01:21:55.680 --> 01:21:56.180
Slam.

1528
01:21:56.360 --> 01:21:56.580
Yeah.

1529
01:21:56.600 --> 01:21:57.000
Push back.

1530
01:21:57.420 --> 01:21:57.660
Yeah.

1531
01:21:58.060 --> 01:22:00.260
I mean, that's some quick reflexes, Phyllis.

1532
01:22:00.560 --> 01:22:00.780
Yeah.

1533
01:22:01.300 --> 01:22:03.320
Because Andy is looking for it everywhere.

1534
01:22:03.320 --> 01:22:05.360
He cannot find it anywhere.

1535
01:22:05.760 --> 01:22:11.880
Well, while Andy's looking for his phone, Angela goes into Michael's office, like Pam suggested, and she says, listen,

1536
01:22:12.420 --> 01:22:21.240
the reason Dwight was late that morning was because he was dropping off the quarterly tax forms that she forgot to send.

1537
01:22:22.400 --> 01:22:25.240
And to be fair, Kevin never reminded her.

1538
01:22:25.780 --> 01:22:30.360
She just wants Michael to know that if Kevin had done his job, she could have done her job better.

1539
01:22:31.100 --> 01:22:33.120
But that Dwight was saving the day.

1540
01:22:33.260 --> 01:22:35.800
He wasn't going for some weird corporate power grab.

1541
01:22:36.020 --> 01:22:38.200
He was doing this favor for her.

1542
01:22:39.060 --> 01:22:39.500
Yes.

1543
01:22:39.820 --> 01:22:44.400
I remember in this scene, Greg gave me the note to, you know, I'm coming in there.

1544
01:22:44.520 --> 01:22:48.740
I'm very nervous because I really don't want people in the office to know my business.

1545
01:22:48.740 --> 01:22:52.860
I don't want them to know who I'm dating, even though I really care for Dwight.

1546
01:22:52.860 --> 01:22:55.820
I just hate the idea of being office gossip, you know?

1547
01:22:56.520 --> 01:23:02.180
So I'm going in there and he said, Angela, just deliver those lines like at the top.

1548
01:23:02.340 --> 01:23:06.500
Like you're just quickly spilling it all out, you know?

1549
01:23:06.600 --> 01:23:06.720
Yeah.

1550
01:23:06.840 --> 01:23:12.240
So that's why I went in with that energy of just like, like if she didn't say it right away, she was going to lose her nerve.

1551
01:23:12.580 --> 01:23:13.900
So I was like, Dwight went to New York.

1552
01:23:14.000 --> 01:23:14.800
He dropped off the tax of her.

1553
01:23:14.980 --> 01:23:16.680
Like, you know, just kind of like throw it out.

1554
01:23:16.840 --> 01:23:17.080
Yes.

1555
01:23:17.080 --> 01:23:21.840
And then, thank God, Michael is such an idiot.

1556
01:23:22.120 --> 01:23:23.600
He doesn't connect the dots.

1557
01:23:23.820 --> 01:23:29.900
He's like, oh, my God, Dwight, if he would do that for anyone in this office, who else is like that, you know?

1558
01:23:30.020 --> 01:23:30.180
Yes.

1559
01:23:30.260 --> 01:23:31.140
And I'm like, no one.

1560
01:23:31.500 --> 01:23:33.360
And Angela's so happy.

1561
01:23:33.600 --> 01:23:40.000
She's so happy she was able to sort of set the record straight without revealing their relationship.

1562
01:23:40.220 --> 01:23:40.480
Yes.

1563
01:23:41.040 --> 01:23:46.540
Michael just takes this as a sign of Dwight's undying loyalty to the company.

1564
01:23:47.160 --> 01:23:47.640
Yeah.

1565
01:23:48.120 --> 01:23:51.000
So he's like, I have to go get him back.

1566
01:23:51.240 --> 01:23:52.600
I have to go get him back.

1567
01:23:52.700 --> 01:23:52.860
Yeah.

1568
01:23:53.140 --> 01:24:03.840
But as he's on his way out the door, Andy, like, jumps in front of him and pitches him like this weekend date that they're going to go on.

1569
01:24:05.830 --> 01:24:08.650
He's like, blurts out a gazillion things.

1570
01:24:08.870 --> 01:24:10.670
And Michael is like, just stop.

1571
01:24:10.870 --> 01:24:11.130
Stop.

1572
01:24:11.390 --> 01:24:12.210
You're driving me crazy.

1573
01:24:12.370 --> 01:24:17.270
And Andy's like, oh, I'm sorry if my friendship is annoying you.

1574
01:24:17.750 --> 01:24:20.190
Sorry, I annoyed you with my friendship.

1575
01:24:20.510 --> 01:24:21.670
Oh, that's what it is.

1576
01:24:22.110 --> 01:24:23.170
That's what it is.

1577
01:24:23.530 --> 01:24:26.290
Well, we had a fan question from Allie White.

1578
01:24:26.590 --> 01:24:32.090
She wanted to know if that list of activities was scripted or improvised by Ed HelMs.

1579
01:24:32.230 --> 01:24:34.170
Guys, it was all scripted.

1580
01:24:34.410 --> 01:24:35.450
Ed memorized that.

1581
01:24:35.690 --> 01:24:37.150
That was not an improvisation.

1582
01:24:38.090 --> 01:24:41.110
It was perfect because they all sounded like a horrible evening.

1583
01:24:42.290 --> 01:24:44.810
Michael's like, I don't want to do any of those things.

1584
01:24:46.510 --> 01:24:48.690
So now Andy's phone starts ringing.

1585
01:24:48.890 --> 01:24:53.050
So he's just been rejected publicly in front of the whole bullpen by Michael.

1586
01:24:53.050 --> 01:24:55.690
And now his phone is ringing again.

1587
01:24:55.830 --> 01:24:58.050
And the man snaps.

1588
01:24:58.330 --> 01:24:59.390
He loses it.

1589
01:24:59.750 --> 01:24:59.970
Yes.

1590
01:25:00.150 --> 01:25:04.070
And this is what we talked about with Ed, where he had to punch a hole in the wall.

1591
01:25:04.990 --> 01:25:13.350
And Angela, I reached out to Kent to find out exactly how many walls we had prepared for this stunt.

1592
01:25:13.610 --> 01:25:14.690
And it was how many?

1593
01:25:15.070 --> 01:25:15.270
Four.

1594
01:25:16.070 --> 01:25:17.230
So we could have done four.

1595
01:25:17.310 --> 01:25:19.410
But remember, Ed thought they only had to do it twice.

1596
01:25:20.010 --> 01:25:21.650
But there were four chances.

1597
01:25:21.850 --> 01:25:31.190
So that's why when we were talking with Ed, I was like, my memory of this scene was that we all had to have our, you know, game face on.

1598
01:25:31.250 --> 01:25:33.310
So we didn't ruin one of these takes.

1599
01:25:33.470 --> 01:25:35.030
We only had four walls, everybody.

1600
01:25:35.590 --> 01:25:42.330
Well, I noticed in the reaction pass in the accounting department, there's one reaction pass where Oscar is standing.

1601
01:25:42.530 --> 01:25:44.350
And then it cuts back and he's like seated.

1602
01:25:44.530 --> 01:25:45.170
And then it cuts back.

1603
01:25:45.390 --> 01:25:47.770
So it was like it didn't quite match up.

1604
01:25:47.770 --> 01:25:49.550
But my kids loved that.

1605
01:25:49.710 --> 01:25:51.870
They're like, Oscar sitting, Oscar standing, Oscar sitting.

1606
01:25:52.250 --> 01:26:01.570
And while all of this is happening, the thing they really were tickled by is that the Homer Simpson doll was turned sideways with like his butt in the air.

1607
01:26:02.070 --> 01:26:03.470
Oh, Homer fell over.

1608
01:26:04.110 --> 01:26:05.170
Homer fell over.

1609
01:26:05.330 --> 01:26:08.530
And then we had to go back and look for when Homer was upright.

1610
01:26:08.530 --> 01:26:11.890
And he was on his side pretty much the whole episode, just so you guys know.

1611
01:26:11.890 --> 01:26:15.090
Oh, guys, the name of this episode is Homer fell over.

1612
01:26:15.990 --> 01:26:17.330
And snow and sadness.

1613
01:26:18.190 --> 01:26:25.350
So now we go outside and Michael's in the parking lot and his car has filled with snow.

1614
01:26:25.510 --> 01:26:26.350
How's he going to get in it?

1615
01:26:26.450 --> 01:26:27.630
He's got to like shovel it out.

1616
01:26:27.710 --> 01:26:30.270
He's rushing, but he has to dig the snow out firSt.

1617
01:26:31.150 --> 01:26:33.310
Angela, I have a wonderful tidbit about this snow.

1618
01:26:33.930 --> 01:26:34.410
What?

1619
01:26:34.410 --> 01:26:41.670
Okay, Kent told me the same snow company filled that Sebring with fake snow, but it wasn't icy snow.

1620
01:26:41.850 --> 01:26:45.490
It was like the little plastic flakes because there's lots of different kinds of fake snow.

1621
01:26:45.630 --> 01:26:47.430
So they were these little plastic flakes.

1622
01:26:48.570 --> 01:26:55.810
And at the end of the shoot day, it took them the entire next day to vacuum all of the snow out.

1623
01:26:55.910 --> 01:26:57.210
And that was a rental.

1624
01:26:57.510 --> 01:26:58.590
They rented that car.

1625
01:26:58.850 --> 01:27:00.710
They had to get all that out of there.

1626
01:27:00.710 --> 01:27:03.970
Yeah, and at the end of the season, they kept it for the whole year.

1627
01:27:04.110 --> 01:27:13.730
At the end of the season, when they returned it, the snow was still in like the inner workings of the car.

1628
01:27:13.930 --> 01:27:19.010
He said whenever they would turn on the AC, snow would blow out of the vents.

1629
01:27:19.230 --> 01:27:19.590
Oh, gosh.

1630
01:27:19.870 --> 01:27:22.310
They never could get all the snow out.

1631
01:27:22.450 --> 01:27:25.770
And I think they had to pay a fee when they returned it.

1632
01:27:26.150 --> 01:27:27.430
I'm sure they did.

1633
01:27:27.430 --> 01:27:34.510
I'm sure they did because someone is going to rent it, turn on the air, and these little fake pieces of plastic snow are going to fly out at them.

1634
01:27:34.710 --> 01:27:34.970
Yes.

1635
01:27:35.250 --> 01:27:36.590
I loved that tidbit.

1636
01:27:36.750 --> 01:27:40.570
I loved that every time we tried to turn on the AC, snow would come out of there.

1637
01:27:40.670 --> 01:27:42.990
Well, Michael has now, he's at Staples.

1638
01:27:43.130 --> 01:27:44.550
He's going to go up to Dwight.

1639
01:27:44.610 --> 01:27:45.530
He's going to apologize.

1640
01:27:45.530 --> 01:27:47.110
He wants him to come back.

1641
01:27:47.970 --> 01:27:51.270
And I love this scene so much.

1642
01:27:51.430 --> 01:27:54.050
I mean, Dwight is tearing up.

1643
01:27:54.270 --> 01:27:55.850
It is a very bromance moment.

1644
01:27:55.850 --> 01:27:56.970
Well, yes.

1645
01:27:57.210 --> 01:27:59.310
That is what Greg calls it.

1646
01:27:59.490 --> 01:28:01.670
He calls it the bromance moment.

1647
01:28:02.430 --> 01:28:09.230
And, you know, playing underneath this scene is the song from An Officer and a Gentleman.

1648
01:28:09.390 --> 01:28:09.750
Yes.

1649
01:28:09.930 --> 01:28:19.230
Remember at the end of Officer and a Gentleman where she's in the factory working and Richard Gere walks in and he scoops her up and they kiss and everyone cheers?

1650
01:28:19.910 --> 01:28:21.150
It's, what is it?

1651
01:28:21.210 --> 01:28:24.170
It's love lift us up where we belong.

1652
01:28:24.410 --> 01:28:24.690
Yes.

1653
01:28:24.710 --> 01:28:24.810
Right?

1654
01:28:24.810 --> 01:28:25.210
Yes.

1655
01:28:25.890 --> 01:28:28.190
Where the eagles fly the whole thing.

1656
01:28:28.450 --> 01:28:35.250
Well, there is like a Muzak version of this playing at Staples during this scene.

1657
01:28:35.430 --> 01:28:36.130
It's amazing.

1658
01:28:36.510 --> 01:28:41.690
Guys, Greg sent in an audio clip talking about this bromance.

1659
01:28:41.690 --> 01:28:49.430
The ending of the return was like the big bromance moment between Michael and Dwight.

1660
01:28:50.350 --> 01:28:54.470
I'm pretty sure the officer and a gentleman was in the script to begin with.

1661
01:28:54.470 --> 01:29:07.030
But as I recall, we were building towards that moment to see Michael going through the aisles at Staples and trying to, you know, make a big romantic moment out of it.

1662
01:29:07.030 --> 01:29:09.950
Like Richard Gere returning for Debra Winger.

1663
01:29:10.590 --> 01:29:12.750
And that is exactly what it is.

1664
01:29:12.950 --> 01:29:17.170
I really wish Rain had picked Steve up and told him around.

1665
01:29:17.170 --> 01:29:18.830
I wish that had been in the script.

1666
01:29:19.410 --> 01:29:22.190
Well, Rain is Debra Winger in this scenario now.

1667
01:29:22.310 --> 01:29:24.350
I know, but he's bigger than Steve.

1668
01:29:24.650 --> 01:29:35.230
So I think it would be like, that's how they, instead of them disappearing, like with him taking his Staples uniform off, that he just carries Michael out.

1669
01:29:35.590 --> 01:29:36.010
Anyway.

1670
01:29:36.790 --> 01:29:43.310
Well, speaking of his uniform, when Dwight comes back to the party at Dunder Mifflin, he's wearing a Battlestar Galactica sweatshirt, right?

1671
01:29:43.930 --> 01:29:44.470
Yeah.

1672
01:29:44.770 --> 01:29:46.750
Okay, you know what about this?

1673
01:29:46.890 --> 01:29:50.910
That Battlestar Galactica did not have any sweatshirt merchandise.

1674
01:29:51.310 --> 01:29:52.170
Isn't that insane?

1675
01:29:52.790 --> 01:29:53.390
Yeah.

1676
01:29:53.430 --> 01:30:00.730
So our wardrobe designer, Carrie Bennett, had to make up a Battlestar Galactica merch sweatshirt for Dwight to wear.

1677
01:30:01.210 --> 01:30:02.650
Yes, they made it special.

1678
01:30:02.650 --> 01:30:03.830
It doesn't exiSt.

1679
01:30:05.230 --> 01:30:07.810
I texted Rain and asked him if he still has it.

1680
